  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Environmental Security Seminar 01-24</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &quot;Environmental Security Workshop&quot; will have academic scholars and government officials from all over the world discussing various aspects of the environment in their own countries and world trends. Each participant will present their paper during the workshop as a speaker; these papers will be published at the conclusion of the conference. Such topics covered will be: Connection of Climate with Military Conflicts; Sustainable Development; Energy Transitions; Developing World&apos;s Challenges; Urban and Rural Perspectives; Weaponization of Resources; Country Case Studies; and Inclusivity &amp; Multilateralism. All discussions within NESA seminars are unofficial in nature, strictly off the record, not for attribution and follow Chatham House Rule. Participants are free to use the information received, but neither the identity nor the affiliation of the speakers, nor that of any other participant, may be revealed for the discussions during the seminar. Only the papers with the names and affiliations of participants will be published.</narrative>
  </description>
